People who plan to purchase an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> can go through the "Get Ready" process starting on Monday, October 12. The new detail was added to the <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/buy-iphone/iphone-duo">iPhone Duo product page</a> yesterday, <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/iPhoneDuo/comments/1wslk7x/on_1210_you_will_be_able_to_get_ready_your_duo/">according to Reddit</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-get-ready.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1067837" /><br/>
Get Ready lets users select a preferred color and capacity, confirm their carrier status, choose accessories, choose an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/applecare/">AppleCare</a>+ plan, select a trade-in, add a payment method, and set a shipping and billing address.<br/>
<br/>
When pre-orders go live, Get Ready is helpful because it allows for one-tap ordering. It will be especially beneficial for the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; because supplies are expected to be limited.<br/>
<br/>
Pre-orders could sell out within minutes given reports of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/29/iphone-duo-reportedly-facing-production-problems/">production issues</a> leading to supply constraints, and users who have Get Ready will be able to submit orders faster.<br/>
<br/>
